00:05:36.566 --> 00:05:40.746
The power bottleneck those new cells are built to break is this episode's engineering

00:05:40.746 --> 00:05:46.146
deep dive, because orbital compute is an electricity problem before it is a software problem.

00:05:46.786 --> 00:05:51.846
Each satellite has to generate and store enough electricity to run inference or training accelerators

00:05:51.846 --> 00:05:55.486
while surviving the thermal cycling and radiation of low-earth orbit.

00:05:56.006 --> 00:06:00.906
And heterojunction stacks do that by layering materials with different band gaps, so the

00:06:00.906 --> 00:06:05.766
cell captures a wider slice of the solar spectrum and throws off less waste heat that would

00:06:05.766 --> 00:06:07.626
otherwise demand a heavier radiator.

00:06:08.226 --> 00:06:13.686
Above the atmosphere, the solar constant is about 1,366 watts per square meter.

00:06:14.346 --> 00:06:18.946
A typical terrestrial reference spectrum is on the order of 1,000 watts per square meter,

00:06:18.946 --> 00:06:24.106
air, so space offers more raw light and no clouds than the orbit takes a cut back.

00:06:24.566 --> 00:06:29.326
A low-earth orbit lasts roughly 90 minutes and the vehicle spends on the order of 30 minutes

00:06:29.326 --> 00:06:33.946
of that in eclipse, which means the array must cover the daylight compute load and still

00:06:33.946 --> 00:06:35.946
top up batteries before the next shadow.

00:06:36.706 --> 00:06:42.566
Silicon's band gap sits near 1.1 electron volts, so a single junction silicon cell dumps

00:06:42.566 --> 00:06:44.286
a large infrared tail as heat.

00:06:44.286 --> 00:06:50.166
Ordinary silicon cells often sit near 20% conversion, as a back-of-envelope figure,

00:06:50.686 --> 00:06:55.866
and a heterojunction stack that converts roughly 25% of the light still turns about three-quarters

00:06:55.866 --> 00:07:00.226
of every incoming watt into heat that can leave a spacecraft only by radiation.

00:07:01.026 --> 00:07:06.646
Raise efficiency a few points and you cut radiator area, cut structure, and raise specific power.

00:07:07.266 --> 00:07:11.646
Watts per kilogram, which is the figure that decides whether extra accelerators are

00:07:11.646 --> 00:07:17.146
the array that feeds them. Fewer defects from an integrated process raise yield, and yield

00:07:17.146 --> 00:07:22.486
is what shrinks the idiot index. How many times the finished space-qualified cell costs over

00:07:22.486 --> 00:07:28.926
the magic wand inputs of a silicon wafer, aluminum, and silver paste? For space-solar that index

00:07:28.926 --> 00:07:34.426
has historically sat on the order of 10 to 100, because inspection, radiation, qualification,

00:07:34.426 --> 00:07:40.026
and broken waifers are paid for by the cells that survive. Drive the gap down, and the marginal

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:45.026
cost of each additional watt in orbit falls toward those raw materials, which is what

00:07:45.026 --> 00:07:49.566
makes a sustained orbital compute cluster look like a manufactured commodity instead of

00:07:49.566 --> 00:07:50.686
a one-off demonstration.

00:07:51.446 --> 00:07:54.726
For SPCX, a modest gain of under 1%.

